 BCE Campanian mercenaries, the Mamertines, seized Messana and killed or expelled many citizens. Their appeal to Rome in 264 BCE triggered the First Punic War. The city became Roman Messana and is today Messina.","ru":["Anaxilas"],"re":"Greek religion","la":"Ancient Greek","img":"/images/states/zancle.jpg","cr":{"a":"Alexander Hoernigk","l":"CC BY 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Messina_2003.JPG"}},"zaporozhian-sich":{"img":"/images/states/zaporozhian-sich.jpg","cr":{"a":"Germenfer","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Zaporizhian_Sich.svg"}},"ziyadid-dynasty":{"img":"/images/states/ziyadid-dynasty.jpg","cr":{"a":"H. Grobe","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jemen1988-022_hg.jpg"}},"zengid-dynasty":{"img":"/images/states/zengid-dynasty.jpg","cr":{"a":"naturalearthdata.com, offered to the Public Domain per Terms of Use","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zengid_territory.png"}},"zhou-wu-sangui":{"img":"/images/states/zhou-wu-sangui.jpg","cr":{"a":"Author in Qing Dynasty","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wu_Sangui.jpg"}},"zhongshan":{"img":"/images/states/zhongshan.jpg","cr":{"a":"EditQ","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%81%87%E6%97%A5%E5%B9%BF%E5%9C%BA.jpg"}}}